title: Start
---
<<declare $found_torn_ticket = false as bool>>
<<declare $found_statement = false as bool>>
<<declare $presented_evidence = "" as string>>
Narrator: The court is in session. We should look around for anything useful before the testimony begins.
<<jump InvestigationIntro>>
===

title: InvestigationIntro
---
Narrator: Click the evidence around the room to collect what you can.
Narrator: The torn ticket and the witness statement are both relevant.
===

title: Object_TornTicket
---
Narrator: A torn train ticket. The date is still legible: the night of the crime.
<<set $found_torn_ticket to true>>
===

title: Object_Statement
---
Narrator: A witness statement with a hurried signature. It mentions the suspect near the station entrance.
<<set $found_statement to true>>
===

title: Testimony_1
---
Judge: Mr. Wright, what is your explanation for the suspect being seen near the station at 9:15 PM?
Witness: I saw the suspect, but I cannot say for certain who it was.
Witness: The real clue is the ticket stub from the station.
<<set $presented_evidence to "">>
<<open_evidence_menu>>
<<if $presented_evidence == "torn_ticket">>
    Witness: Ah, the torn ticket! That matches the station timings.
    <<jump Testimony_1_Refute>>
<<else>>
    Witness: That's not it. Try again.
    <<jump Testimony_1>>
<<endif>>
===

title: Testimony_1_Refute
---
Narrator: The witness falters. The ticket proves the suspect was at the station, contradicting the earlier claim.
Narrator: The testimony advances.
===

